---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { upstreamIssues, STATUS_LABEL } from "../data/upstream";

const description =
  "How every format tin is checked against the reference implementation of the format it speaks, and the upstream bugs that turned up along the way.";
---

<Base title="Correctness" description={description}>
  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="wrap wrap--wide">
      <p class="eyebrow">Correctness</p>
      <h1 class="section-title">Gated on someone else's implementation</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A format library that only passes its own tests has proved nothing, so I gated every
        format tin here against the reference implementation of the format — in both
        directions where the format has two.
      </p>

      <div class="proofs">
        <div class="proof">
          <h3>Iceberg</h3>
          <p>
            Row-sets <strong>cell-exact against PyIceberg 0.11.1 and DuckDB 1.5.5</strong>
            across <strong>48 of 48 filter cases</strong>, in both directions, including
            deletes, deletion vectors and schema evolution. Tables magmalake writes are read
            back cell-exact by both — and PyIceberg can append to a table magmalake created.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="proof">
          <h3>Parquet</h3>
          <p>
            Value-exact against pyarrow on 33 fixtures — every value of every column — and
            pyarrow reads back every file magmalake writes. The Arrow export imports through
            <code>pyarrow.Array._import_from_c</code>.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="proof">
          <h3>Avro &amp; Thrift</h3>
          <p>
            Avro round-trips against fastavro both ways across all four codecs. Thrift is
            <strong>byte-identical to Apache Thrift</strong> on generated wire vectors, in
            both the compact and the binary protocol.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="proof">
          <h3>S3 &amp; SigV4</h3>
          <p>
            <strong>37 of 37</strong> cases of the official AWS SigV4 test suite, every stage.
            S3 is verified end-to-end against MinIO <strong>in CI</strong>, not only on a
            developer's machine.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="proof">
          <h3>Roaring</h3>
          <p>
            Byte-exact against pyroaring in both directions, with pyroaring-produced payloads
            baked into the tests as constants so the oracle cannot drift.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="proof">
          <h3>Everything else</h3>
          <p>
            Codecs against Python <code>zstandard</code>, <code>lz4</code>,
            <code>brotli</code> and <code>python-snappy</code>; hashes against zlib, mmh3 and
            xxhash plus the Iceberg spec's own vectors; threads against contended-count and
            memory-visibility proofs.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="upstream">
        <h3 class="upstream__title">Building it found bugs upstream</h3>
        <p class="upstream__blurb">
          Holding three implementations against each other surfaces disagreements, and not all
          of them turned out to be my fault. I cut each one below down to a standalone script
          or unit test with no magmalake code in it, then either reported it upstream or —
          where someone had got there first — matched it to the report that already existed.
        </p>
        <ul class="upstream__list">
          {
            upstreamIssues.map((u) => (
              <li>
                <a class="upstream__head" href={u.url} rel="noopener">
                  <span class="upstream__project">{u.project}</span>
                  <span class="upstream__ref">{u.ref}</span>
                  <span class:list={["upstream__tag", `upstream__tag--${u.status}`]}>
                    {STATUS_LABEL[u.status]}
                  </span>
                </a>
                <span class="upstream__bug">{u.bug}</span>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .proofs {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(100%, 290px), 1fr));
    gap: 1px;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    background: var(--border);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .proof {
    background: var(--surface);
    padding: 1.4rem 1.5rem;
  }
  .proof h3 {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--lake);
  }
  .proof p {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .proof strong { color: var(--text); }

  .upstream {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--ember) 28%, var(--border));
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--ember-wash);
    padding: 1.6rem 1.7rem;
  }
  .upstream__title {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.45rem;
  }
  .upstream__blurb {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    max-width: 72ch;
    margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
  }
  .upstream__list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 240px), 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .upstream__list li {
    border-left: 2px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--ember) 45%, transparent);
    padding-left: 0.85rem;
  }
  .upstream__head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.4rem 0.55rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .upstream__head:hover .upstream__ref { text-decoration: underline; }
  .upstream__project {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ember);
  }
  .upstream__ref {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .upstream__tag {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.625rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 0.1rem 0.4rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
    color: var(--text-faint);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .upstream__tag--filed {
    color: var(--ember);
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ember) 45%, transparent);
  }
  .upstream__bug {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
</style>
